# ============================================================
# flow/mst_shared_leg_prefix.buda
#
# Two MST edges leaving ONE block along the same axis.
#
# `realize_mst_edge` routes each edge on its own, from the
# closest point between its two blocks.  Two edges incident on
# the same block therefore start at the SAME face point, and if
# both go L-shaped with the same first axis, the shorter one's
# leg lies entirely inside the longer one's.
#
# The longer leg's first stretch is then a duplicate, and its
# start is a FREE END: the shorter leg owns the block tap, and
# nothing joins the long leg until the two diverge.
#
# Nothing downstream removed it.  The ANTENNA rule counts
# attachment POSITIONS and the long leg has two elsewhere, so it
# passes; #514's tap-overhang rule wants the piece to lie over a
# block the segment itself taps, and this one taps nothing.
#
# What it DID do is push the leg's end past the junction where
# the edges diverge, turning that junction from an endpoint conn
# into a mid-span one — and DetailedNUTS only snaps a bit to its
# own via at an ENDPOINT conn, so every bit kept the shared
# abstract end instead of stopping at its own via.
#
# Found on flow/rnr/mix2_topdown_refine bundle 35
# (TRUNK_V+MST@x690), where the trunk and a branch both left
# chip/i_dnuts1_4/v0 at x=2130 heading west:
#
#   seg3  H (2130,1020)->(2110,1020)   edge 1, owns the tap
#   seg5  H (2130,1020)->( 980,1020)   edge 2, runs over it
#
# and seg5's bits carried 8.75 + 5.75 + 2.75 units past their
# last via — with `check_design` reporting Success.
#
# FIXED — but OPT-IN, default off (`set_trim_mst_legs on`, below;
# corpus-wide `BUDA_MST_LEG_TRIM=1`).  The cut is sound geometry,
# yet candidates are WL-SORTED, so shortening one RE-SORTS the
# pool and changes which candidates clear generation gates:
# measured on chip3_topdown, 9 of 640 bundles change selected
# topology TYPE and 3 change pool SIZE (control, main twice: 0),
# and leaf bundles elsewhere lose tracks — 260 -> 636 unplaced.
# The search space moves, not the wire.  Same reason
# set_prune_dominated / set_dedup_loci / set_drop_dangling are
# opt-in, and the same caveat: it renumbers candidate indices, so
# select_topology pins must come from an opted-in run.
#
# The trim cuts each leg back to where it stops being a
# duplicate (`trim_shared_leg_prefixes`).  Connectivity is
# preserved by construction: the cut point is the shorter leg's
# far end, which is either that edge's own BEND or a block FACE,
# so something is always waiting at the seam.  On bundle 35:
#
#   seg5  (2130,1020) -> (2110,1020)   the duplicated prefix, gone
#   detailed WL 13753 -> 13736         exactly the dangling metal
#   check_design       dirty -> Success
#
# This vehicle is the SHAPE on its own, so the mechanism has a
# home that does not depend on a 100-bundle hier design keeping
# one particular candidate at one particular index.  Four blocks
# is the minimum for a standalone MST candidate.  It reproduces
# on BOTH standalone strategies -- measured on main, at the
# shared corner (2010,1010) after the corner margin:
#
#   MST_HV  seg1 len  120 inside seg3 len 1320
#   MST_VH  seg3 len   70 inside seg1 len  620
#
# and neither survives the trim.
#
# Run:  bin/buda flow/mst_shared_leg_prefix.buda --no-viz
# ============================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 33.33
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 33.33

corner_margin dx 10 dy 10

# `hub` is the shared MST node.  Both targets sit BEYOND its
# south-west CORNER, so closest_points
# returns that same corner for each: the two edges start at one point.
# Each is then an L that goes WEST first, and `near`'s short west leg
# lies inside `far`'s long one.
add_block hub   2000 1000  2100 1100
add_block near  1800  300  1900  400
add_block far    600  900   700  950

# The MST must keep BOTH as direct edges off hub rather than chaining
# near--far, so the blocks are placed to make that the cheaper tree:
#   hub--near  100 + 600 =  700      hub--far  1300 + 50 = 1350
#   near--far 1100 + 500 = 1600   <- dearer than either, so no chain
add_block up    2000 1800  2100 1900

add_bus d[4] hub.tx near.rx,far.rx,up.rx

run_bundler strict

# The trim is OPT-IN (default off, byte-identical): it re-sorts the
# WL-ordered candidate pool, so it moves selection well beyond the
# bundle it fixes.  Declared BEFORE generation, as it must be.
set_trim_mst_legs on
generate_topologies
run_planner 1
run_nuts

def_track_pattern 4 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4
def_track_pattern 5 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4

run_detailed_nuts
dump_topologies --conn
check_design dnuts
report_wirelength
